# LF everywhere, on every platform.
#
# Prettier writes LF (its default), the index already holds LF, and the CI
# runners are Linux. Without this file, a Windows checkout with
# core.autocrlf=true expects CRLF on disk, so every file Prettier had touched
# showed as modified with no content change — ten or more of them at a time,
# permanently, which buried real changes in `git status` and made `git add -A`
# dangerous. This overrides autocrlf for this repository only.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets: never touched by line-ending conversion.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
